(text "LDO - LM1084  |  Texas Instruments  |  29V 5A adjustable LDO, TO-263" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 14.00 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1e594d8d-f1c4-494b-a395-27fac7f70a54"))
(text "Default build: VOUT = 1.8 V (fixed resistors - no trimmer). Pin-compatible family: pin1 ADJ/SET, pin2 + tab OUT, pin3 IN.\nOther outputs: change only the programming resistor(s) per the VOUT table." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 19.30 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3d8ce5b1-2aab-403d-9377-260b3b24b13c"))
(text "DESIGN EQUATIONS - LM1084 (TI LM1084 datasheet SNVS037H)\nDesign point: VOUT 1.8 V (default), VIN 5.0 V nominal (3.3 V rail also checked), IOUT rated 5.0 A, TO-263-3 (KTT)\nOutput: VOUT = VREF*(1 + R2/R1) + IADJ*R2 ; VREF = 1.25 V, IADJ = 55 uA typ (120 max)\n  Min-load rule: VREF/R1 >= IMIN = 10 mA max -> R1 <= 125 ohm ; R1 = 121 ohm (divider current 10.3 mA)\n  R2 = (VOUT - VREF)/(VREF/R1 + IADJ) = 53.0 ohm -> 53.6 ohm (E96) ; VOUT = 1.8067 V (+0.37%)\n  IADJ error at IADJ max = 6.4 mV ; VREF tolerance +/-1% (25C) / +/-2% (full temp) dominates\n  R1 dissipation = VREF^2/R1 = 12.9 mW ; R2 = 5.8 mW (0603 OK)\nPSRR: ripple gain = VOUT/VREF = 1.44 -> PSRR degrades 3.2 dB without CADJ\n  CADJ > 1/(2*pi*f*R1): 120 Hz -> 11.0 uF ; 100 kHz post-regulator -> 13.2 nF\nDropout: VDO = 1.5 V max @ 5 A -> VIN(min) = VOUT + VDO = 3.30 V at full load\n  3.3 V rail: headroom 1.50 V vs VDO 1.5 V -> NOT OK at full load (use 5 V input) ; 5 V rail: headroom 3.20 V -> OK\nCurrent limit: 5.5 A min / 8 A typ (VIN-VOUT = 5 V) ; VIN(max) = 29 V\nCapacitors: Needs ESR zero: 10 uF tantalum or 50 uF Al (22 uF tant / 150 uF Al if CADJ fitted).\n  Pure MLCC output not recommended.\nTHERMAL (thetaJA = 40.4 C/W, KTT JEDEC; TJ(max) 125 C)\n  VIN 5.0 V: efficiency = VOUT*IOUT/(VIN*(IOUT+Idiv)) = 36% (max VOUT/VIN = 36%) ; temp rise dT = thetaJA*PD = 646 C\n  VIN 5.0 V: PD = (VIN-VOUT)*IOUT = 3.20*5.0 = 16.00 W -> TJ = 671C @25C / 731C @85C ; thermal IOUT(max) = 0.58 A @TA50C, 0.31 A @TA85C\n  VIN 3.3 V: efficiency = VOUT*IOUT/(VIN*(IOUT+Idiv)) = 54% (max VOUT/VIN = 55%) ; temp rise dT = thetaJA*PD = 303 C\n  VIN 3.3 V: PD = (VIN-VOUT)*IOUT = 1.50*5.0 = 7.50 W -> TJ = 328C @25C / 388C @85C ; thermal IOUT(max) = 1.24 A @TA50C, 0.66 A @TA85C\n  PD(max) = (125 - TA)/thetaJA = 1.86 W @50C, 0.99 W @85C. Add copper / heatsink or pre-regulate to raise current." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 130.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fe7cfa7c-7861-4ece-93b8-2f50b6c3e055"))
